[size=5][b]Valheim Builder Planner[/b][/size]
[i]Plan your builds outside the game, then rebuild them in your world — 100 % vanilla.[/i]

[b]Not a mod:[/b] a separate program for Windows that runs on its own, next to the game. Your game, your saves and your achievements are not touched.
[b]No game files included:[/b] on first launch the planner reads the building pieces from [b]your own[/b] Valheim installation (about a minute), on your computer.

[size=4][b]What it does[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Every Hammer piece[/b] (around 390) with its real shape, size, cost and crafting station — names in the game's 36 languages
[*][b]Snapping like in the game[/b]: same snap points and rules, rotation in 22.5° steps, manual snap point choice
[*][b]Stability with the game's rules[/b] (wood, core wood, stone, iron, marble, ashstone…): blue → green → red, and a warning when something would collapse. The preview tells you before you place a piece.
[*][b]Floor view[/b]: top-down plan floor by floor, with the pieces and materials of each floor
[*][b]Rebuild guide[/b]: the plan in build order (floors → poles → walls → doors → beams → roof → furniture), the current step glows in 3D. Go back and forth freely.
[*][b]Materials list[/b] and a [b]build list export[/b] (checklist to keep on a second screen)
[*]Copy/paste, undo, autosave, save/open plans, Valheim-style flying camera
[*]Norse-style interface with piece thumbnails
[/list]

[size=4][b]Two ways to get your build into the game — you choose[/b][/size]
The planner never changes your game. Once your plan is ready, there are two ways to rebuild it in your world:

[size=3][b]1. Vanilla, by hand — achievements stay ON[/b] [color=#7ec850](recommended, nothing to install)[/color][/size]
You play Valheim normally and rebuild the plan yourself with the hammer, following the planner:
[list]
[*]keep the planner open next to the game (second screen, or Alt+Tab);
[*]press [b]B[/b] for the [b]rebuild guide[/b]: it shows your plan step by step (floors, then poles, walls, roof…) and highlights in 3D the pieces of the current step;
[*]the [b]floor view[/b] (P) and the [b]materials list[/b] tell you exactly what to place and what to gather.
[/list]
No mod, no file copied into the game: [b]your game stays 100 % vanilla and your achievements keep working.[/b]

[size=3][b]2. With the PlanBuild mod — faster, but achievements are OFF while it is installed[/b][/size]
For players who already use mods. [url=https://thunderstore.io/c/valheim/p/MathiasDecrock/PlanBuild/]PlanBuild[/url] is a separate mod (not made by me) that shows a plan [b]inside the game[/b] as see-through "ghost" pieces, so you only have to fill them in.
[list]
[*]In the planner: [i]Export ▾ → PlanBuild blueprint[/i] sends your plan to PlanBuild in one click (manual install, r2modman and Thunderstore profiles are detected).
[*]In game: the Blueprint Rune places the ghost pieces, you build them with your own materials.
[/list]
[color=#e0b85a][b]Important:[/b] Valheim turns achievements off as long as [u]any[/u] mod is loaded (PlanBuild needs BepInEx and Jotunn). It does not damage your save: remove or disable the mods and achievements work again.[/color]

[b]Both ways:[/b] you can also [b]open PlanBuild (.blueprint) and BuildShare (.vbuild) files[/b] shared by the community in the planner, check their cost and stability, then rebuild them either way.

[size=4][b]Install[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Download and unzip anywhere (keep the folder together).
[*]Run [b]ValheimBuilderPlanner.exe[/b] (Windows 10/11, 64-bit).
[*]Click [b]Read my game[/b]. Valheim is found through Steam automatically, or choose its folder.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Controls[/b][/size]
Tab: menu / mouse · Mouse: look · WASD (ZQSD on AZERTY): fly · Space/C: up/down · Left click: place · Wheel or R: rotate · Middle click: remove · Shift+middle click: pick a piece · Ctrl+C / Ctrl+V: copy/paste · Ctrl+Z: undo · P: floor view · V: stability · B: guide

[size=4][b]Languages[/b][/size]
Piece names follow the game (36 languages). Interface: English and French — translations welcome on GitHub.

[size=4][b]Source code[/b][/size]
Open source (MIT): [url=https://github.com/ICCUser/valheim-builder-planner]github.com/ICCUser/valheim-builder-planner[/url]

